id: pmc-x49u
title: Add tag-aware fallback dates for release-gated changelogs
description: "GitHub issue #120: a release-gated package with no tag falls back to the current UTC date, so changelog checks drift daily; the existing --date override then masks a real tag date once publication occurs. Add a fallback-only date contract, optionally derived from CalVer, whose value is ignored whenever an authoritative tag timestamp exists."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: determinism,github-issue,release-context
created_at: "2026-08-11T23:41:20.016Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T23:08:18.481Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-16T22:51:50.827Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-16T22:51:50.827Z"
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A fallback date is used only when no release tag resolves; an eventual tag timestamp always wins; CalVer-derived fallback behavior is explicit and tested; CLI, SDK extension flags, docs, 100/100/100 coverage, release checks, and installed-package acceptance pass."
reviewer: codex
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Added --date-fallback and --date-from-version to standalone generate, SDK generate, and SDK export. Existing tag timestamps remain authoritative and bypass fallback-value validation; mutually exclusive fallback flags fail closed on every invocation, while an invalid CalVer fallback fails closed only when no tag resolves and the fallback would be consumed. Documentation and real packed-install acceptance are included."
expected_result: "Untagged releases generate stable, validated fallback dates without an unconditional override; a later tag automatically becomes authoritative and bypasses unused fallback-value validation."
actual_result: Literal and CalVer fallbacks are stable and validated before tagging; existing tag dates supersede them without evaluating an unused CalVer fallback; mutually exclusive flags still fail closed; 387-test exact coverage passes; and the packed extension generated and exported the expected pm-rust heading.
