comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T23:41:20.016Z",codex,"Duplicate check: exact-title and all-status searches found no canonical item for GitHub issue #120. pmc-vdss addresses UTC timezone drift, not daily clock drift in intentionally tagless packages; pmc-7dm6 covers authoritative tag dates. This open item owns the missing fallback-only contract."
  "2026-08-16T22:51:50.422Z",codex,"Packed pm-changelog 2026.8.16, installed that tarball through pm package install into a disposable copy of the real pm-rust tracker, and verified both pm changelog generate and export produced 0.1.0-alpha.1 dated 2026-08-08. The source pm-rust checkout remained clean; disposable data was removed."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T22:51:50.422Z",codex,"Implemented literal and CalVer-derived no-tag fallbacks with explicit precedence: --date override, existing tag date, fallback, then current UTC date."
  "2026-08-16T22:53:38.593Z",codex,"Authoritative release:check passed after closure: typecheck; 143 documented declarations; 387 tests; 100/100/100 across all 9 measured source files; zero production vulnerabilities; pack dry run; deterministic changelog check."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T22:51:50.422Z",codex,A fallback contract must defer not only its value but also its validation until the authoritative tag is absent; otherwise a tagged SemVer release can fail on a CalVer-only fallback it never consumes.
